needs -Pet, which the battery does not pass. Measured 2026-07-29: WITH -Pet the watchdog panics, dumps and halts with IF=0 in 1.3s, so it is not an infinite loop and the old reason saying so was wrong. WITHOUT -Pet it hangs past 90s, because wd-stale-threshold-progress is 5500000 ticks at ticks-per-second 18, about 3.5 days. Even given -Pet it cannot carry an .expected: the dump is R=/S=/H=/HWM=/STK= addresses that move with every codegen change, the same reason the .fatal tests have none.
